DAY 40 - PART A: THEORY
etcd Backup/Restore and Cluster Upgrades
Time: 40 minutes
==================================================================

PART 1: BACKUP AND RESTORE
==========================

1. WHAT TO BACK UP
------------------
  etcd snapshot             ALL cluster state (objects)
  /etc/kubernetes/pki       certificates and keys (CA!)
  your manifests / Helm values / Git repo
NOT in etcd: data inside PersistentVolumes. Back those up separately
(volume snapshots, Velero, application dumps like Day 27).

Velero: popular tool that backs up Kubernetes objects AND volume
snapshots to object storage; used for migrations and DR.


2. SNAPSHOT
-----------
  ETCDCTL_API=3 etcdctl snapshot save /backup/etcd.db \
    --endpoints=https://127.0.0.1:2379 \
    --cacert=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/ca.crt \
    --cert=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/server.crt \
    --key=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/server.key
  etcdutl snapshot status /backup/etcd.db -w table


3. RESTORE (single control plane, kubeadm)
------------------------------------------
  1. Stop the API server and etcd: move their manifests out of
     /etc/kubernetes/manifests
  2. etcdutl snapshot restore /backup/etcd.db --data-dir /var/lib/etcd-restore
  3. Point etcd.yaml's hostPath (etcd-data volume) to /var/lib/etcd-restore
  4. Move the manifests back; kubelet starts them
  5. Restart kubelet; verify objects
Everything created after the snapshot is gone; things deleted after
it come back.


PART 2: UPGRADES
================

4. RULES
--------
- One MINOR version at a time: 1.33 -> 1.34 -> 1.35 (no skipping).
- Control plane first, then workers.
- kubelet may be up to 3 minors OLDER than the API server, never newer.
- Read the release notes (removed APIs!) before upgrading.


5. kubeadm UPGRADE STEPS
------------------------
Control plane node:
  1. change package repo to the new minor (pkgs.k8s.io/.../v1.34)
  2. upgrade kubeadm only
  3. kubeadm upgrade plan
  4. kubeadm upgrade apply v1.34.x   (static pods, certs renewed,
                                       CoreDNS/kube-proxy upgraded)
  5. drain the node, upgrade kubelet + kubectl, restart kubelet,
     uncordon
Each worker, one at a time:
  1. repo + kubeadm upgrade
  2. kubeadm upgrade node
  3. drain from control plane, upgrade kubelet + kubectl, restart,
     uncordon

Managed clouds do the control plane for you and roll node pools
(Week 7), but the rules (one minor at a time, deprecated APIs,
PodDisruptionBudgets) still apply.


KEY POINTS TO REMEMBER
----------------------
- etcd snapshot + PKI = cluster state; PV data needs its own backup.
- Restore = stop, restore to new dir, repoint, start.
- Upgrade one minor at a time; control plane first; drain nodes.
